From df4ae306481abc62aede02508fe335ff0d091f0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ga=C3=ABl=20Duval?= <gael@murena.io>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 13:40:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] feat(documenteditor): Word Font and Paragraph dialogs

- Font dialog (Font group launcher, Ctrl+D): Font tab with font, font
  style and size as a text box over a list (typing selects the first
  match), font colour, underline style and colour, effects
  (strikethrough, double strikethrough, superscript, subscript, small
  caps, all caps, hidden, mutually exclusive as in Word); Advanced tab
  with scale, spacing and position (Normal/Expanded/Condensed,
  Normal/Raised/Lowered, by n pt), kerning and OpenType ligatures;
  rendered preview of the selected text. Only the changed values are
  applied, in one undo step. Underline styles other than single,
  underline colour, scale, kerning, number forms and stylistic sets are
  shown disabled: the engine does not support them.
- Paragraph dialog (Paragraph group launcher): the paragraph settings of
  the editor laid out like Word, with two top tabs, "Indents and
  Spacing" (General, Indentation, Spacing, Preview) and "Line and Page
  Breaks" (Pagination, Formatting exceptions, Preview), and a Tabs...
  button that applies the dialog then opens the tab stops alone in a
  Tabs dialog. All logic stays in ParagraphSettingsAdvanced.
- Modify Style > Format > Font... opens the Font dialog for the style.
The launcher cases for font and paragraph move from the Toolbar
controller to DE.Controllers.WordFormatting. Strings in en, fr, de, es,
it, pt, pt-pt, nl, ru, pl, ja, zh.

[branding]

Assisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
